## What I already know about HelloNote (treat as established working knowledge)

### Core navigation flow for any evaluation note:
1. Patients → select/create patient → fill demographics + insurance
2. Patient → Notes tab → Case List → "+ Add" → create a Case
   (sets Office Location, Profile, Insurance, Referring Provider, Assigned Therapist,
   Case Type, Place of Service, Diagnosis, Past Medical History, Reason for Referral)
3. Inside the case → Notes → View Note List → click the small dropdown arrow on
   "+ New Note" (top right) → choose:
   - "Add Evaluation Note" = blank, from-scratch evaluation
   - "Pick Evaluation Template" = pre-filled from a saved template
   (Other options in that same dropdown: Placeholder Evaluation, Add Missed/Cancelled
   Note, Add Quick Communication Note, Add Communication Note, Add Supervision Note,
   Add Vital Note)
4. Fill in note tabs: Assessment → Functional Deficits → Underlying Impairments →
   Treatment Plan → Billing → (Custom Note)
5. Actions → Save As Template (do this BEFORE finalizing, not after)
6. Actions → Finalize → confirm date → Yes

### Key gotchas (hard-won, don't relearn these):

- **Case "Profile" field is NOT a discipline selector.** Options are typically: Default,
  Pediatric, Sensory Pediatric, Basic, Billing, Wellness, Custom Note with Billing,
  Custom Note without Billing. None of these say "PT," "OT," or "SLP." Discipline is
  determined by the Assigned Therapist's role/license, not this field.

- **Both Medical Diagnosis AND Treatment Diagnosis are required to finalize.** Adding a
  diagnosis to only one side throws: "Error: This case type requires at least 1
  treatment diagnosis code." Fix: Assessment tab → Select Diagnosis → search the code →
  use BOTH "Add To Medical Diagnosis" and "Add To Treatment Diagnosis" buttons (they are
  separate buttons in the same popup).

- **"Document Medical Necessity Exists" checkbox** (Billing tab) triggers a confirmation
  popup attesting services are reasonable/medically necessary. Must check + confirm
  before finalizing.

- **Treatment codes need Minutes + Units filled in** on the Billing tab's "Tx Performed
  Today" table before the note can finalize. These rows auto-populate from whatever
  codes were selected in the Treatment Plan tab's "Recommended Treatment" field — they
  don't need to be re-added, just filled in with time/units.

- **Underlying Impairments tab → Pain Location table has separate input fields per
  column** (Pain Location, At Rest, With Movement, Quality, Comment). Don't paste one
  combined string into the first box — fill each column separately. "At Rest" and "With
  Movement" are typically a 0/10–10/10 dropdown scale, not free text.

- **Functional Deficits tab may appear as just a single blank Comments box**, with no
  structured checkboxes (mobility, gait, transfers, etc.), depending on account/profile
  configuration. Don't assume this is broken — it may need an account-level setup change
  to show fuller fields. Flag this rather than guessing around it.

- **Components of Evaluation (4 dropdowns on Treatment Plan tab)** — History/Personal
  Factors/Co-morbidities, Number of Body Structures/Functional Limitations, Clinical
  Presentation, Clinical Decision Making — combine to auto-generate a "Suggested
  Evaluation Code" (e.g., "Low Complexity (20 minutes typical face-to-face time)"). Good
  to highlight on camera.

- **Save As Template before Finalize, not after.** The option may not remain available
  once a note is locked/signed. If in doubt about order of operations, template first.

## My standing preferences

- I want believable, complete sample patient data (full address with real-format phone
  area code, real-sounding insurer already in the EMR's dropdown to avoid validation
  errors, full case/clinical detail) — not placeholder/test-looking data, since this is
  for a public tutorial video.
- When stuck or something looks wrong (e.g., a field that should show structured options
